# Paired with canonical_reduced.bvnr: the same quantities spelled with prefixes
# and with a repeated base. `bovnar pretty-print --canonical` must fold both to
# byte-identical output -- that convergence is the whole claim of the mode.
#
# NOTE the float_dec value. Its trailing zeros are SIGNIFICANT in that family,
# so 0.250 and 0.25 are not interchangeable and the canonical form deliberately
# does not collapse them. Both files therefore write 0.25: the mode canonicalises
# how a unit is SPELLED, not how much precision a decimal claims.
.dist  = <float:64,k~m> 5.0;
.area  = <float:64,m·m> 2.0;
.speed = <float:64,k~m/h> 90.0;
.mass  = <float_dec:64,k~g> 0.25;
